WEBVTT Example

NOTE
Second-line messages for Blu-ray mode. Copy files like this one into
/home/emanspeaks/bluray_cues/ and pick one from the web page on port 8080.

Timestamps are elapsed play time as the player reports it, i.e. counting from
the moment the title started playing -- not from the start of the disc. The
display is 20 columns wide; anything longer is clipped. Stick to plain ASCII:
the panel is not a UTF-8 device, and a multi-byte character eats more than one
column and renders as garbage.

Cues are only drawn once you press "Start cues" on the web page. The player
reports elapsed time and nothing else, so nothing here can tell the feature
apart from a menu loop or a trailer.

You can edit this file while a disc is playing: it is checked once a second and
reloaded when it changes. If a save leaves it unparseable, the previously loaded
cues stay up and the error goes to the service log, so fix and save again.

NOTE
A cue identifier line (like "opening" below) is optional and is ignored.

opening
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:40.000
OPENING TITLES

NOTE
End times are exclusive: this one clears the line at exactly 1:47:55.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:30.000
FIRST ACT

01:47:30.000 --> 01:47:55.000
TEARS IN RAIN

01:52:00.000 --> 01:53:00.000
THE END
